Class OpenAIClient:
- implement the BaseLLMClient contract against OpenAI's chat completions HTTP API
- support plain text generation plus JSON-schema constrained generation for structured run outputs
- emit SSE-compatible text deltas for streaming preview text
- normalize usage metadata into the shared LLMUsage shape
- reuse the same debug logging style as Gemini so model IO stays inspectable in local development

Method generate_text:
- build the chat completion payload from system + user prompts
- attach JSON schema response_format when the caller requests application/json
- post to the OpenAI API
- extract the assistant text and token usage

Method stream_text:
- send a streaming chat completion request
- parse SSE data lines
- yield shared text_delta events for preview text
- finish with one completed event carrying normalized usage

Method _build_payload:
- map the backend prompt contract into OpenAI chat-completions request fields
- optionally attach strict json_schema response formatting
- enable stream usage reporting for streaming mode

Method _extract_text / _extract_stream_delta / _normalize_content:
- normalize OpenAI content fields into plain strings for the rest of the backend

Method _extract_usage:
- map prompt/completion tokens and elapsed latency into LLMUsage
